  "last_updated_by": "Portal",
  "centroid_northing": 6718128,
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "title_number": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<div>The combination of the first floor rear extension, dormer and hip-to-gable roof extension would introduce a complexity to the roof form.&nbsp;Their relationship&nbsp;would create an incongruous appearance which does not have regard to the built form of the host dwelling or surrounding area. It would appear at odds with local character and would not reflect the modesty of the existing dwellings within the immediate vicinity.&nbsp; The proposal is therefore contrary to:</div><ul><li><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"\">National Planning Policy</span>&nbsp;Framework\r\n(NPPF) (December, 2024)</li><li>Policy D4 of the\r\nLondon Plan (March 2021)</li><li>The Residential\r\nExtensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)</li><li><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"\">Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of </span>The Barking and\r\nDagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)</li></ul>",
    "<div>The scale, siting and design of the proposed development would result in an increased sense of overbearingness and a harmful loss of outlook and daylight to neighbouring occupiers, therefore constituting unneighbourly development and contrary to:</div><div><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\"><br></span></div><ul><li><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp;</span>(NPPF) (December, 2024)</li><li><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">Policy\r\nD4 of the London Plan (March 2021)</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">&nbsp;The Residential\r\nExtensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012);</span></li><li><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of </span>The London Borough of Barking and\r\nDagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)</li></ul>"
  ],
